# Craterhoof Behemoth, ruling 2025-04-04: "The value of X is calculated only once, as Craterhoof Behemoth's last ability
# resolves." Turn 3 Bot1 casts it (five Moxen and a Black Lotus) with an Ornithopter already in play. With the enters trigger
# on the stack Bot2 exiles the Behemoth with Swords to Plowshares (Bot1 gains 5 life, its power then). The ability still
# resolves, but Bot1 controls one creature, the Ornithopter: X is 1, so it is a 1/3 with trample, not the 2/4 it would be
# were the Behemoth counted.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Craterhoof Behemoth
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Swords to Plowshares
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Craterhoof Behemoth.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Craterhoof Behemoth)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 25
Exile = Craterhoof Behemoth
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Trample
